#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kate is using two different forms of plugins, namely plugins for the &kate; application and plugins for the &kate; editor component. The latter are available to any application using the editor component, such as KDevelop, Quanta, Kile, Kwrite and many others, while application plugins are specific to the &kate; application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can enable both types of plugins in the <link linkend=\"configuring-kate-configdialog\">configuration dialog</link>, which also provides access to additional configuration options for plugins that requires that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are many plugins for various purposes available and you can search the web for more. A few plugins are shipped with the editor component, for inserting automatic braces, insert files, data tools and exporting text as &HTML;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editor Component Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel> tab on the <guilabel>Extensions</guilabel> page lists all available plugins and you can check those you want to use. Click on the <guibutton>Information</guibutton> button to open the <guilabel>About</guilabel> dialog of this plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once a configurable plugin is checked, the <guibutton>Configure</guibutton> button is enabled and you can click it in order to configure the highlighted plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "AutoBrace"
msgstr "Auto-Klemmen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "The autobrace plugin supersedes the &kate; internal <quote>Auto Brackets</quote> feature. It automatically inserts a closing brace <keycap>}</keycap> at the beginning of the next line after ending a line with an opening one <keycap>{</keycap> and pressing the &Enter; key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Data Tools"
msgstr "Datenwarktüüch"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enables data tools like thesaurus and spell check (if installed). Data tools are only available when text is selected, or when the right mouse button is clicked over a word. If no data tools are offered even when text is selected, you need to install them. Some data tools are part of the &koffice; package. If this plugin is enabled and data tools are installed, additional items appear at the end of the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Exporter</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "This command allows you to export the current document with all highlighting information into a HTML document using <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export as HTML</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Additionally you can use <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy as HTML</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to copy the currently selected text as HTML to the system clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "IconInserter"
msgstr "Lüttbild infögen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "The icon inserter plugin is only of use for &kde; developers: It adds an item <guimenuitem>Insert KIcon-Code</guimenuitem> into the context menu of the editor. If activated, the &kde;'s icon chooser opens (showing application icons, action icons &etc;..). If you click on it, the file name without file extension will be inserted as text. Useful only for setting icons via &kde;'s framework through the KIcon() class."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insane (not ZEN) HTML coding (light edition)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "A plugin, which does zen-coding like selector completion. For more information see <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zen_Coding\"> Zen Coding</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert File"
msgstr "Datei infögen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "This plugin allows you to insert any readable file at the cursor position. If enabled, the <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> menu has an additional menu item <guimenuitem>Insert File</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; Application Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; plugins are additional functions for the &kate; editor. They can add extra menus and shortcuts, and extend &kate;'s features. You can install as many or as few as you like, from within &kate;. Open &kate;'s configuration dialog with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kate;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Application</guimenu><guimenuitem>Plugins</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to choose the wanted plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "The available application plugins are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-findinfiles\">Find in files tool view</link> - Toolview allowing to search in all open files or files in the filesystem"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "GDB - Provides a simple GDB frontend"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backtrace Browser - Backtrace navigation tool view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-quickswitcher\">Quick Document switcher</link> - Quickly switch to another already opened document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "SQL Plugin - Execute query on SQL databases"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search Plugin - Find a pattern in files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab Bar - Adds a standard tab bar to &kate;'s main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Filter - Easy text filtering"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Symbol Viewer - Extract and show reference symbols from source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-fsbrowser\">File system browser</link> - File system browser tool view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Terminal tool view - Toolview embedding a terminal widget"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "CTags Plugin - Look up definitions/declarations with CTags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-filetemplate\">File Templates</link> - Create new files from templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open Header - Opens the corresponding .h/[.cpp|.c] file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link>External Tools</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Build Plugin - Compile or Make and parse error messages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-mail\">Mail files</link> - Send files via email"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multiline Tab Bar - Add a tab bar with multiple rows to &kate;'s main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kate Snippets - Snippets plugin with code completion support"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Jovie Text-to-Speech Plugin - Adds a menu entry for speaking the text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-xmlcheck\">&XML; Validation</link>- Validates &XML; files using xmllint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugin-xmltools\">&XML;Completetion</link> - Lists &XML; elements, attributes, attribute values and entities allowed by DTD"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tabify - Adds a tab bar to Kate's main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Templates"
msgstr "Dateivörlagen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "The File Templates plugin allows you to create files based on other files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you first install Kate, you need to enable the plugin:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Kate</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the tree on the left of the screen, click <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the <guilabel>Plugin Manager</guilabel> panel on the right, select <guilabel>File Templates</guilabel>, and then click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can now use any file as a template (this creates a copy of the file with an empty &URL;.) Special template files can contain macros to fill in information such as your name, email address, the current date, and position the cursor at a convenient position in the new file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can easily create a new template from an open document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Templates that you save to the template folder are listed under the menu item <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "The template folder is part of the &kde; file system, and consists of at least"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/applications/kate/plugins/katefiletemplates/templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/share/applications/kate/plugins/katefiletemplates/templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "If your <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> environment variable contains additional directories, those are searched for a similar subdirectory as well. If equally named templates are found, the one in the local (KDEHOME) folder is chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:275 plugins.docbook:577 plugins.docbook:693
#: plugins.docbook:770 plugins.docbook:803 plugins.docbook:847
#: plugins.docbook:1086 plugins.docbook:1130 plugins.docbook:1165
#: plugins.docbook:1346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu Structure"
msgstr "Menüopbuu"

#. Tag: menuchoice
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>New From Template</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Any File...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Presents you with Open File dialog that allows you to use any file as a template. If the chosen file has the extension <filename>katetemplate</filename> it will be parsed for template information and macros."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New From Template</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "The remainder of submenus contains links to templates. Click a menuitem to create a file as described by the menu item text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Manage Templates...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will launch a dialog with a list of all templates found within the template directories, along with options to add, edit or remove templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a &kate; Template"
msgstr "En &kate;-Vörlaag bruken"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "When creating a file from a template that contain template macros, some macros appears as editable variables in the text. Such variables appears as underlined words in the text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "The first variable will be selected, so you just have to type to edit it. If the document text contains more instances of the same variable, they are changed as you edit. To move to the next editable variable, press the TAB key. When the last variable is edited, the list is dropped, and your TAB key works as normal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating your own templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "To create a new template, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Manage Templates</guimenuitem></menuchoice> Item to launch the template management dialog. In that, click <guibutton>New...</guibutton> to launch the File Template Wizard. You will be asked for an optional file to turn into a template and prompted for template information settings, and a template file will be created for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "Alternatively, you can create a template manually by adding template information to the top of any file, add text and macros, and save it with the <filename>katetemplate</filename> extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid "The template menu gets automatically updated if you chose to store your template in the template directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing templates"
msgstr "Bewerken vun Vörlagen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "To edit a template, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Manage Templates...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Select the template you want to work on and click <guibutton>Edit...</guibutton>, and the template file will be opened. Close the dialog, edit the template file as desired, save it and close it. Changes to templates takes immediate effect, you can activate the template to test your changes after saving it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kate; Template Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you use files with the extension <filename>katetemplate</filename>, they will be parsed for template information, macros and a cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "While reading in the file, the parser keeps lines beginning with the phrase <constant>katetemplate:</constant> and searches them for template information in the form VARIABLENAME=VALUE. The first line not starting with <constant>katetemplate:</constant> will be taken as the start of the template contents. VALUE may contain any character but equal sign (=). Legal variable names are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template"
msgstr "Vörlaag"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the template name, displayed in the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group"
msgstr "Koppel"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "The group places the template in a submenu of the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Naam"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the name that will be set for the document, and displayed in the file list and title bar. If the name contains <userinput>%N</userinput> that will be replaced with a number, increasing if more documents has the same name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight"
msgstr "Rutheven"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "The plug-in will try to set the Highlight for the new document to the value of this variable. The value should be the name, as found in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Highlighting</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Beschrieven"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "A short informative description of the template. This is currently used to set a Whatsthis string for the menu item, but may be used for more purposes in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Author"
msgstr "Autor"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "A string identifying the author, for example in the form <userinput>Name &lt;email address&gt;</userinput>. This is currently used to set a Whatsthis string for the menu item, but may be used for more purposes in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template Macros"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: plugins.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "While parsing the template contents, macros in the form <userinput>%{NAME}</userinput> or <userinput>${NAME}</userinput> are expanded. If you use the <userinput>$</userinput> prefix, the expanded macro will be treated as a editable variable when a document is created from the template, whereas if you use <userinput>%</userinput> it is not, unless expanding failed."
msgstr ""

